From dc3f96a90fc4ac11c73b8809eff4dd909aea4138 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:28:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] BananaDS perf: render.3d_share and render.3d_wait2d at 1x
 too

At render.scale=1 every line showing the 3D layer copied Gengis's line into the 2D job (1 KB, up to 192 KB a
frame on the emulator's thread) and GetLine made the emulator's thread wait for the line's bin, or draw it.
Both settings applied only at 2x (the quarter functions were set only then). Now the 1x line goes the same way:
the job points at the frame's own row (Gengis keeps two frames' rows: QuarterRows, no X scroll, no aborted
frame) and, with render.3d_wait2d and unit A on the 2D thread, that thread waits for the line's bin. The copy
and the wait stay where they were otherwise (display capture, X scroll, no 2D thread). Same pictures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PvbFhKAw3ERk5a13S651g1
